<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνομ-αστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>skilful at naming,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				424a
			</span></i> ; <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to naming,</i> hence
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τέχνη ἡ ὀνομαστική</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				423d
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> alone, ib.<i><span class="en">
				425a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτῶσις</span>) the <i>nominative</i> case, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.1.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				636.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				107.4
			</span></i>(pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιβλίον</span>) <i>vocabulary,</i> arranged acc. to the
			subjects, and not alphabetically as in a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεξικόν,</span> such as the work of <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i> Pollux : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κά, τά,</span> title of work by <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				26a
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>by a special name,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					14.646a
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>in the nominative case,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				4.4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
